WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.760
I want to take up in volume 3 and begin at January the 22nd, 1900, and this is about

2
00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:14.720
our response to grace.

3
00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:20.360
After going through most bitter days of privation, Louisa said, "My poor heart was struggling

4
00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:26.920
between the fear of having lost Jesus and the hope that who knows I might see him again."

5
00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:33.600
Oh God, what a bloody war this poor heart of mine has to bear.

6
00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:42.200
The pain is so great that now at one stage it would be ice cold and then it would be

7
00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:47.200
squeezed as though under a press and would drip blood.

8
00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:52.160
While I was in this state I felt my sweet Jesus near me.

9
00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:57.320
He removed a veil from me which prevented me from seeing him.

10
00:00:57.320 --> 00:01:04.740
So finally I was able to see him, immediately I said to him, "Lord, you don't love me anymore."

11
00:01:04.740 --> 00:01:09.120
Now when Louisa gives this kind of response to Jesus, it's very personal and it's to

12
00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:14.360
do with these awful privations that she has to learn how to cope with.

13
00:01:14.360 --> 00:01:21.480
If you put beside this Jeremiah 31-3 where God says, "I have loved you with an everlasting

14
00:01:21.480 --> 00:01:27.100
love and my love is constant, it never changes."

15
00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:31.360
But Louisa has to learn how to deal with this privation.

16
00:01:31.360 --> 00:01:38.700
Jesus said, "Yes, yes, what I recommend to you is response to my grace.

17
00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:46.120
And in order to be faithful, you must be like the echo that resounds in an empty space."

18
00:01:46.120 --> 00:01:52.680
Now the significant thing here is the empty space because throughout these writings Jesus

19
00:01:52.680 --> 00:01:58.680
tells us that the only safe place for us to be in if we want to grow spiritually and

20
00:01:58.680 --> 00:02:07.200
we want God to work in us and produce fruit in us is that we must sink into our nothingness,

21
00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:11.960
that we must be utterly and completely convinced of our nothingness.

22
00:02:11.960 --> 00:02:18.640
And the more we stay in the nothingness, the more He can work with us.

23
00:02:18.640 --> 00:02:22.720
So He said, "You must be like an echo that resounds in an empty space.

24
00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:28.000
As soon as a voice is emitted immediately and without the slightest hesitation, one can

25
00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:31.320
hear the echo booming after it.

26
00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:37.120
In the same way, as soon as you begin to receive my grace without even waiting for me to finish

27
00:02:37.120 --> 00:02:43.240
giving it, begin immediately the echo of your response.

28
00:02:43.240 --> 00:02:49.880
So He's asking for heroic correspondence to grace here from Louisa.

29
00:02:49.880 --> 00:02:54.480
And I want to give you two Corinthians 12, nine in case you think it's impossible which

30
00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:55.580
it is.

31
00:02:55.580 --> 00:02:57.920
My grace is sufficient for you.

32
00:02:57.920 --> 00:03:01.160
My power works best in weakness.

33
00:03:01.160 --> 00:03:03.920
So we don't have any excuse.

34
00:03:03.920 --> 00:03:07.240
We only have to throw ourselves on the Lord."

35
00:03:07.240 --> 00:03:16.960
So January 27, 1900, and this speaks about the order of the virtues in the soul.

36
00:03:16.960 --> 00:03:21.640
Louisa says, "I continue to be almost without my sweet Jesus.

37
00:03:21.640 --> 00:03:24.160
My life is leaving me because of the pain.

38
00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:29.960
I feel such tedium, boredom, and tiredness of life.

39
00:03:29.960 --> 00:03:36.240
Now if you understand that she's sitting in a bed doing a nothing, you will understand

40
00:03:36.240 --> 00:03:41.760
that when she says she's suffering from tedium and boredom and tiredness of life, that is

41
00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:44.040
probably an understatement.

42
00:03:44.040 --> 00:03:48.560
I would go mad if I was in her position."

43
00:03:48.560 --> 00:03:55.560
So Louisa said, "I kept saying in my interior, 'Oh how my exile has been prolonged, oh what

44
00:03:55.560 --> 00:04:01.440
happiness would be mine, if I could loosen the bonds of my body so that my soul might

45
00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:04.900
take wing and fly towards its highest good.'

46
00:04:04.900 --> 00:04:12.240
Now that's Sam 55, 'Oh that I had the wings of a dove, I would fly away and be at rest.'

47
00:04:12.240 --> 00:04:15.920
Of course Louisa is not going to die until 1947.

48
00:04:15.920 --> 00:04:18.480
She's another 47 years to go.

49
00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:21.280
So she has to get used to this privation.

50
00:04:21.280 --> 00:04:28.400
A thought said to me, 'And what if you go to hell?'

51
00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:33.720
And Louisa, 'So as not to call the devil to fight me,' she said, immediately snapped

52
00:04:33.720 --> 00:04:39.760
out of it by saying, 'Well then even from hell I would send my sighs to my sweet Jesus

53
00:04:39.760 --> 00:04:42.080
and even from there I'd love him.'

54
00:04:42.080 --> 00:04:46.540
Now that's a direct response from the last message I've just given you, in which Jesus

55
00:04:46.540 --> 00:04:50.480
said, 'Your response to grace must be immediately immediate.'

56
00:04:50.480 --> 00:04:56.920
So here she says, 'I snapped out of it quickly,' she realized it was a temptation.

57
00:04:56.920 --> 00:05:01.760
So while I was amid these and other thoughts she said, 'The story would be too long if

58
00:05:01.760 --> 00:05:06.800
I told you the whole lot, beloved Jesus made himself seen for just a little and with this

59
00:05:06.800 --> 00:05:11.640
serious aspect he told me, 'Your time has not yet come.'

60
00:05:11.640 --> 00:05:19.000
For that I want to give you John 2-4 and John 7-6, when Jesus said of himself, 'My hour

61
00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:23.040
has not yet come.'

62
00:05:23.040 --> 00:05:30.320
So if the hour hasn't come, Louisa has to learn how to penetrate the meaning of this

63
00:05:30.320 --> 00:05:34.320
privation and make the most of it.

64
00:05:34.320 --> 00:05:40.040
Then with an intellectual light he made me understand that everything must be orderly

65
00:05:40.040 --> 00:05:41.280
in the soul.

66
00:05:41.280 --> 00:05:49.120
This intellectual light is called infused knowledge, it comes directly from him.

67
00:05:49.120 --> 00:05:56.800
The soul possesses many little apartments, this infused knowledge told her, in which

68
00:05:56.800 --> 00:06:02.160
each virtue takes its place, even though it can be said that one single virtue contains

69
00:06:02.160 --> 00:06:07.720
all the others within itself, and that the soul by possessing only one of them comes to

70
00:06:07.720 --> 00:06:10.080
be endowed with them all.

71
00:06:10.080 --> 00:06:18.680
However, in spite of this they are all distinct, so much so that each of them has its own place

72
00:06:18.680 --> 00:06:20.920
in the soul.

73
00:06:20.920 --> 00:06:28.360
And here is how the virtues have their origin in the mystery of the most holy trinity.

74
00:06:28.360 --> 00:06:32.400
While the most holy trinity is one, there are three distinct persons and while they

75
00:06:32.400 --> 00:06:36.720
are three they are one.

76
00:06:36.720 --> 00:06:43.240
Louisa said, 'I also understood that these apartments in the soul are either full of virtue

77
00:06:43.240 --> 00:06:49.480
or full of vice, the opposite of that virtue.'

78
00:06:49.480 --> 00:06:56.760
And if there is neither virtue nor vice, the soul is empty of a terrible emptiness.

79
00:06:56.760 --> 00:07:02.920
It seems to me that they are like a house, the soul is like a house, which contains many

80
00:07:02.920 --> 00:07:05.280
rooms all empty.

81
00:07:05.280 --> 00:07:12.040
Now, Jesus said in John 14 verses 1 and 2, 'In my Father's house there are many rooms

82
00:07:12.040 --> 00:07:15.000
and there is one for you.'

83
00:07:15.000 --> 00:07:20.920
But here the Lord is showing us that inside of our own soul there are many rooms.

84
00:07:20.920 --> 00:07:26.720
And Louisa said, 'She saw that some of the rooms were full of snakes, some of mud.

85
00:07:26.720 --> 00:07:32.680
Mud usually means earthiness and filtiness and that kind of stuff.'

86
00:07:32.680 --> 00:07:37.880
Some were full of pieces of furniture full of dust and some were dark.

87
00:07:37.880 --> 00:07:46.160
'A Lord,' she said, 'you alone can put my poor soul in order.'

88
00:07:46.160 --> 00:07:51.080
You can see therefore that if the rooms have snakes and mud and furniture full of dust

89
00:07:51.080 --> 00:07:56.400
that we have to go and get involved in fighting the good fight.

90
00:07:56.400 --> 00:08:00.200
So for this I want to give you 1 Timothy 6, 12.

91
00:08:00.200 --> 00:08:06.220
This is why we have to fight the good fight and conquer the kingdom that is within us.

92
00:08:06.220 --> 00:08:10.160
We have 2 Timothy 4, 7.

93
00:08:10.160 --> 00:08:17.280
We have Hebrews 10 verses 32 to 35 and Hebrews 11, 37.

94
00:08:17.280 --> 00:08:25.200
But I also want to remind you of a lady called Elizabeth Wang.

95
00:08:25.200 --> 00:08:31.360
She was a convert to Catholicism and the Lord gave her a wonderful gift of painting the

96
00:08:31.360 --> 00:08:33.960
mysteries of our faith.

97
00:08:33.960 --> 00:08:40.760
And you can find them all on radiantlight.org.

98
00:08:40.760 --> 00:08:46.680
And one of these paintings is of a good soul receiving Holy Communion.

99
00:08:46.680 --> 00:08:50.400
I don't know what you would paint if somebody asked you to paint somebody receiving Holy

100
00:08:50.400 --> 00:08:51.400
Communion.

101
00:08:51.400 --> 00:08:55.880
You paint them on the outside, receiving Holy Communion on the tongue, no.

102
00:08:55.880 --> 00:08:59.040
She painted the soul like a womb.

103
00:08:59.040 --> 00:09:05.140
And Jesus was sitting on the edge of the soul looking in with a perplexed expression on

104
00:09:05.140 --> 00:09:07.080
his face.

105
00:09:07.080 --> 00:09:12.240
Because while the soul had received him, there wasn't any room for him.

106
00:09:12.240 --> 00:09:14.560
Now this wasn't a bad person.

107
00:09:14.560 --> 00:09:17.720
But the soul was full of all kinds of junk.

108
00:09:17.720 --> 00:09:22.680
And she painted the junk as boxes, some of them tin and some of them tic and some of

109
00:09:22.680 --> 00:09:25.520
them tall and small and square and round and all the rest of it.

110
00:09:25.520 --> 00:09:27.480
But they were filling the soul.

111
00:09:27.480 --> 00:09:32.480
And these are all the useless things that we allow to clog up our lives.

112
00:09:32.480 --> 00:09:38.080
And that's why we were told in volumes one and two, and we will continue right through

113
00:09:38.080 --> 00:09:44.320
to volume five that the Lord will say to us, "Listen, this is my language, not his.

114
00:09:44.320 --> 00:09:48.720
You've got to get rid of the junk out of your life if you're to make room for God."

115
00:09:48.720 --> 00:09:51.760
Okay, that's my language.

116
00:09:51.760 --> 00:09:52.760
Okay.

117
00:09:52.760 --> 00:09:55.280
So if you've got snakes, you've got to get rid of them.

118
00:09:55.280 --> 00:09:58.000
If you've got mud, you've got to clean up.

119
00:09:58.000 --> 00:10:03.120
If you've got pieces of furniture full of dust, well, do you even want the furniture?

120
00:10:03.120 --> 00:10:05.080
Do you need it?

121
00:10:05.080 --> 00:10:07.480
And so we must fight the good fight.

122
00:10:07.480 --> 00:10:14.480
So in all of these early volumes, we are being told that if we don't get our act together

123
00:10:14.480 --> 00:10:21.640
spiritually, you cannot live the phenomenon and the prodigy of the divine will.

124
00:10:21.640 --> 00:10:26.120
It's not possible you wouldn't be ready.

125
00:10:26.120 --> 00:10:33.720
So you won't be surprised then that the next message in January 28, 1900 is about mortification.

126
00:10:33.720 --> 00:10:40.280
In other words, the clean up, and we're going to have a number of messages about mortification

127
00:10:40.280 --> 00:10:44.920
as we go on.

128
00:10:44.920 --> 00:10:47.400
Louisa says it still continues the same way.

129
00:10:47.400 --> 00:10:50.880
This morning he transported me outside of myself.

130
00:10:50.880 --> 00:10:57.080
Now, usually I say to people that these are out of the body experiences, but the correct

131
00:10:57.080 --> 00:11:03.200
language would be that these are flights of the spirit, which St. John of the Cross speaks

132
00:11:03.200 --> 00:11:10.880
about very marvelously in his works.

133
00:11:10.880 --> 00:11:15.640
And Louisa has these flights of the spirit on a daily basis.

134
00:11:15.640 --> 00:11:21.200
After a long time, I seem to see Jesus with clarity, she said, but I saw myself as so

135
00:11:21.200 --> 00:11:25.560
bad that I did not dare to utter a single word.

136
00:11:25.560 --> 00:11:33.400
Now, the woman who is saying this has already had three mystical marriages with God.

137
00:11:33.400 --> 00:11:37.120
So how can she use the expression so bad?

138
00:11:37.120 --> 00:11:39.160
Louisa is a very young person.

139
00:11:39.160 --> 00:11:40.160
She's Italian.

140
00:11:40.160 --> 00:11:43.200
She's very emotional.

141
00:11:43.200 --> 00:11:49.840
And sometimes this expression, she uses the word cativa in Italian, which means you're

142
00:11:49.840 --> 00:11:52.920
not a little thing is the way it's used.

143
00:11:52.920 --> 00:11:58.360
And it's really a combination of how what where her feelings are at, where her emotions

144
00:11:58.360 --> 00:11:59.360
are at.

145
00:11:59.360 --> 00:12:05.880
It's not a statement of sin because if it was a statement of sin, she could not be in the

146
00:12:05.880 --> 00:12:06.880
divine will.

147
00:12:06.880 --> 00:12:15.240
It's just that simple, one, John, three, two, that those who are living in union with God

148
00:12:15.240 --> 00:12:17.000
don't sin.

149
00:12:17.000 --> 00:12:23.440
And this is going to be a very, very, maybe John one, John three, two to five.

150
00:12:23.440 --> 00:12:25.600
We have to become very, very clear about this.

151
00:12:25.600 --> 00:12:30.440
And that's why in the early volumes, we are told to go to war with sin.

152
00:12:30.440 --> 00:12:34.720
And if we don't go to war with sin, there is no divine will going to take over in us

153
00:12:34.720 --> 00:12:40.760
because sin is horrific to God.

154
00:12:40.760 --> 00:12:43.280
So Louisa said she saw herself very bad.

155
00:12:43.280 --> 00:12:49.880
The other way of explaining that too is that the closer we come to God, the more we see

156
00:12:49.880 --> 00:12:54.240
of the miseries of human nature.

157
00:12:54.240 --> 00:13:00.320
And those of us who have not had that vision don't see clearly, and I want to give you

158
00:13:00.320 --> 00:13:03.400
an example of that.

159
00:13:03.400 --> 00:13:08.840
One day I was driving in a car and it was a very dull rainy day.

160
00:13:08.840 --> 00:13:14.800
And a big lorry overtook me because I wasn't traveling fast at the time and dumped all

161
00:13:14.800 --> 00:13:18.440
its mud on my windscreen.

162
00:13:18.440 --> 00:13:19.440
So no problem.

163
00:13:19.440 --> 00:13:23.000
I cleaned off the windscreen and continued driving.

164
00:13:23.000 --> 00:13:31.480
And I thought the windscreen was clean until the clouds parted, excuse me, and a ray of

165
00:13:31.480 --> 00:13:33.880
sunshine came through.

166
00:13:33.880 --> 00:13:43.320
And it was only as the light increased that I saw a thin layer of traffic film on the

167
00:13:43.320 --> 00:13:47.520
windscreen which made it difficult to drive now.

168
00:13:47.520 --> 00:13:51.480
When it was dark and rainy, it didn't make it difficult to drive.

169
00:13:51.480 --> 00:13:55.560
But once you increased the light, yes, you could see more.

170
00:13:55.560 --> 00:13:58.960
And I had to work really hard to get this traffic film off.

171
00:13:58.960 --> 00:14:04.680
And then the windscreen was crystal clear and the light could come through and I could

172
00:14:04.680 --> 00:14:11.400
experience its warmth and its comfort and its acceptance of me and everything else.

173
00:14:11.400 --> 00:14:18.120
So as the saints get closer and closer to God, they become aware of that traffic film that

174
00:14:18.120 --> 00:14:24.400
we can't see because we're back in a darker place.

175
00:14:24.400 --> 00:14:30.560
So Louisa said, "I saw Jesus with clarity," you see, "the clarity is the light.

176
00:14:30.560 --> 00:14:34.960
And I saw myself as so bad I didn't dare utter a single word," she said.

177
00:14:34.960 --> 00:14:42.360
"We looked at each other, but in silence," that's contemplation.

178
00:14:42.360 --> 00:14:47.600
Through these mutual gazes, I understood that my good Jesus was filled with bitterness,

179
00:14:47.600 --> 00:14:51.440
but I didn't dare to say pour them into me.

180
00:14:51.440 --> 00:14:57.360
He himself drew near and began to pour them, but unable to contain them, as I received

181
00:14:57.360 --> 00:14:59.720
them, I threw them on the ground.

182
00:14:59.720 --> 00:15:03.800
Now, Louisa knows we're in Volume 3.

183
00:15:03.800 --> 00:15:08.720
She knows that if she throws them on the ground, there's going to be chastisement.

184
00:15:08.720 --> 00:15:13.760
If she doesn't swallow them and suffer them, the chastisement won't be mitigated.

185
00:15:13.760 --> 00:15:16.760
So he said to me, "What are you doing?

186
00:15:16.760 --> 00:15:20.600
Do you not want to share in my bitterness anymore?

187
00:15:20.600 --> 00:15:24.240
Do no longer want to give me relief in my pains?"

188
00:15:24.240 --> 00:15:27.560
And Louisa said, "Lord, this isn't my will.

189
00:15:27.560 --> 00:15:30.080
I myself don't know what has happened to me.

190
00:15:30.080 --> 00:15:36.080
I feel so full that I don't know where to contain them.

191
00:15:36.080 --> 00:15:43.320
Only a prodigy of yours can enlarge my interior so that I may receive your bitterness."

192
00:15:43.320 --> 00:15:52.440
So here is the Lord letting Louisa understand that for things that God wants to work in

193
00:15:52.440 --> 00:15:59.080
us, he has to increase our capacity to be able to receive what he's giving to us.

194
00:15:59.080 --> 00:16:03.680
And so he has to give us an experience of our nothingness, of our inability.

195
00:16:03.680 --> 00:16:09.760
So I want to give you John 15.5, "Without me, you can do nothing."

196
00:16:09.760 --> 00:16:14.880
And the more we go on spiritually, the more we are convinced about that, we can do nothing

197
00:16:14.880 --> 00:16:17.160
without him.

198
00:16:17.160 --> 00:16:25.600
So Louisa says, "Jesus marked me with the sign of the cross, and he poured the bitterness

199
00:16:25.600 --> 00:16:27.000
again."

200
00:16:27.000 --> 00:16:29.400
So it seemed I was able to contain them.

201
00:16:29.400 --> 00:16:35.600
And then he said, "My daughter, mortification is like fire that dries up all humours."

202
00:16:35.600 --> 00:16:40.240
Before I go on to that, I want to give you Philippians 4.13.

203
00:16:40.240 --> 00:16:45.800
We had just dealt with John 15.5 that without him I could do nothing.

204
00:16:45.800 --> 00:16:52.480
St. Paul says in Philippians 4.13, "But with Christ I can do all things."

205
00:16:52.480 --> 00:16:58.520
So before Jesus blessed her and enlarged her capacity, she couldn't do it.

206
00:16:58.520 --> 00:17:06.800
In other words, yes, she could, and then Jesus decided to enlighten her about mortification.

207
00:17:06.800 --> 00:17:11.080
Mortification, he said, "Is like fire that dries up the humours."

208
00:17:11.080 --> 00:17:14.960
Now our dictionaries don't use the word "humour" anymore.

209
00:17:14.960 --> 00:17:22.960
It seems to include our moods and our emotions.

210
00:17:22.960 --> 00:17:26.200
You know the way we say, "I got out of bed and I was in a bad mood all day."

211
00:17:26.200 --> 00:17:29.340
And we don't even know why it happens.

212
00:17:29.340 --> 00:17:35.320
So he said that mortification deals with these bad moods.

213
00:17:35.320 --> 00:17:43.440
In the same way, mortification dries up these bad moods, which are present in the soul.

214
00:17:43.440 --> 00:17:48.520
And it inundates her with a sanctifying mood.

215
00:17:48.520 --> 00:17:52.640
In other words, the exact opposite to the bad mood is given to you.

216
00:17:52.640 --> 00:17:57.680
And such a way as to make the most beautiful virtues sprout.

217
00:17:57.680 --> 00:18:04.080
Now this is a very important piece of information because there are days when we say, "We got

218
00:18:04.080 --> 00:18:07.600
out of the wrong side of the bed and we don't know what's wrong with this."

219
00:18:07.600 --> 00:18:09.760
And Jesus is telling us how to deal with it.

220
00:18:09.760 --> 00:18:16.440
So I want to give you two Corinthians 10 verses 4 to 5, where St. Paul says that every thought

221
00:18:16.440 --> 00:18:19.440
must be captured and given to Christ.

222
00:18:19.440 --> 00:18:27.200
So we've got to take ourselves on, and it's only easy if you haven't tried it.

223
00:18:27.200 --> 00:18:33.160
